019f126e-f3af-7c34-bf7b-97912fd17e00 | nonreductionist view → need to integrate → nonmotor symptoms and clinical phenotypes

# sentence: Finally, we stress that the heterogeneous disease progression observed from patient to patient cannot be understood with oversimplified reductionist views.
019f126e-f3af-7c4d-a23f-4939dc6b4a0d | heterogeneous disease progression → cannot be understood with → unidimensional approaches

# sentence: The challenge is to understand the key factors in each case, and to bring this concept to the level of personalized medicine.

# sentence: Resting microglia monitor the local environment and control the response of the immune system.
019f0e7a-1000-7000-0000-000000000001 | resting microglia → monitor → local environment
019f0e7a-1000-7000-0000-000000000002 | resting microglia → control → response of immune system

# sentence: Under minor stress, microglia release anti-inflammatory cytokines and growth factors.
019f0e7a-1100-7000-0000-000000000001 | microglia → release → anti-inflammatory cytokines

# sentence: Under more significant stress, microglia release proinflammatory cytokines to recruit systemic immune cells and toxic factors to kill the pathogen.
019f0e7a-1200-7000-0000-000000000001 | microglia → release → proinflammatory cytokines

# sentence: The interpretation by microglia of a given environmental state makes the difference between beneficial and detrimental outcomes of the immune response.
019f126e-f3af-706a-b60e-2a693c8dc8d6 | interpretation by microglia of environmental state → make difference between → beneficial and detrimental outcomes

# sentence: It remains unclear, however, whether neuroinflammation is purely a side effect of PD, or whether it plays a more causal role in the pathogenesis.

# sentence: It has been demonstrated that neurons can exert feedback control on microglia.
019f126e-f3af-7cab-9f3f-2de78bed1c08 | neurons → exert → feedback control on microglia

# sentence: Many neuronal products, including membrane glycoproteins such as CD22, CD47, and CD200, and neuronal cell adhesion molecules, bind microglia receptors and inhibit microglial activation [97].

# sentence: In the majority of experimental approaches, neuroinflammation is a secondary detrimental effect triggered by PD-related chemical or genetic stress factors [98].
019f126e-f3af-7239-ac38-8184c73724c1 | neuroinflammation → be → secondary detrimental effect triggered by PD-related pathology

# sentence: For example, microglia are able to detect misfolded a-synuclein and increase neurotoxicity through the production of ROS and proinflammatory cytokines [99] [100].
019f126e-f3af-7286-8315-1c8ef8ccfd9a | microglia → detect → misfolded a-synuclein
019f126e-f3af-7b24-903d-1d74ad25afc5 | microglia → increase → neurotoxicity through production of ROS

# sentence: Astrocytes modulate the microglial response and play a supportive role for brain neurons [101] [102].
019f0e7a-1300-7000-0000-000000000001 | astrocytes → modulate → microglial response
019f0e7a-1300-7000-0000-000000000002 | astrocytes → play → supportive role for brain neurons

# sentence: Recent in vitro data suggest that DJ-1 deficiency in astrocytes might deregulate their neuroinflammatory response, thereby contributing to neurodegeneration [103].
019f126e-f3af-7dfe-993c-cfe17d6c87dc | DJ-1 deficiency in astrocytes → deregulate → neuroinflammatory response
019f126e-f3af-7bcb-9f4a-8203d21c0c8a | DJ-1 deficiency in astrocytes → aggravate → DA neuronal death
019f126e-f3af-7dfe-8000-0000000000a6 | recent in vitro data → suggest → 019f126e-f3af-7dfe-993c-cfe17d6c87dc

# sentence: The proportion of astrocytes in the SN is the lowest of any brain area [104].
019f0e7a-1400-7000-0000-000000000001 | proportion of astrocytes in SN → be → lowest of any brain area

# sentence: The high number of microglia promoting neuroinflammation, opposing a low number of regulatory astrocytes, appears to provide a plausible explanation for the elevated risk of neuroinflammation in this brain region.
019f126e-f3af-7230-aed8-1542a11d0b1c | high number of microglia promoting neuroinflammation → promote → susceptibility of SN to PD
019f126e-f3af-7af5-a6cc-56e1532b04e2 | low number of regulatory astrocytes → promote → susceptibility of SN to PD

# sentence: Furthermore, the pigment neuromelanin, which is present in substantia nigra pars compacta neurons, has been shown to activate microglia [105], which further increases the susceptibility of this brain area to neuroinflammation.
019f126e-f3af-7328-bfb1-784f5f3015b1 | neuromelanin → act as → immunogen

# sentence: Finally, there is evidence supporting the idea that the adaptive immune system, as well as the innate immune system, might be involved in PD.
019f126e-f3af-76c7-ae8a-31f81b995b95 | adaptive immune system → be involved in → PD
019f126e-f3af-741e-bb03-539e2dd8720c | innate immune system → be involved in → PD

# sentence: For example, a genetic association has been found between a region of the human leukocyte antigen and PD [106].
019f126e-f3af-7ff4-a201-6276972ee99d | region of human leukocyte antigen → be associated with → PD

# sentence: Responses of the adaptive immune system have been reported near both activated microglia and degenerating neurons, in particular in the substantia nigra pars compacta [107].
019f126e-f3af-7775-84e8-6814a8dd6c8e | responses of adaptive immune system → be reported near → activated microglia
019f126e-f3af-78db-b4f1-16b6f4b45622 | responses of adaptive immune system → be reported near → degenerating neurons

# sentence: Importantly, regulatory T cells have been shown to attenuate nigrostriatal DA neurodegeneration in an MPTP mouse model [108].
019f126e-f3af-7822-9d05-eac5b4e7ba67 | regulatory T cells → attenuate → nigrostriatal DA neurodegeneration in MPTP mouse model

# sentence: Given this plethora of supporting evidence, we believe that neuroinflammation is at least a modulator of disease progression, and that further basic research in this field is needed to form the basis for future developments that target inflammatory pathways for disease-modifying therapies [109]..
019f126e-f3af-7771-8b59-ca28c3aaf588 | neuroinflammation → be → modulator of disease progression in PD

# sentence: Historically, PD research has been driven by medical knowledge.
019f126e-f3af-7eb1-91a2-095c0a55f5a1 | PD research → be driven by → medical knowledge

# sentence: However, neuroscience research based on molecular and cellular biology has added further layers of complexity to our understanding of PD.
019f126e-f3af-7dd5-9fa4-1672a8255906 | neuroscience research → add → further layers of complexity to understanding of PD

# sentence: In turn, increased efforts are required to coordinate and integrate interdisciplinary PD research.
019f126e-f3af-7759-8b82-95fb041cc126 | increased efforts → be required to → coordinate interdisciplinary PD research
019f126e-f3af-7605-bb1b-ff74fd30ea62 | increased efforts → be required to → integrate interdisciplinary PD research

# sentence: The ultimate aim in systems PD biomedicine is to translate mechanistic insights into clinical applications, and to use these to improve patient quality of life [110].
019f126e-f3af-770c-bebb-ce09c31f1b62 | ultimate aim in systems PD biomedicine → be → to translate mechanistic insights into clinical applications

# sentence: One important challenge is the need to develop theoretical models that are able to accurately represent the pathogenesis of PD.
019f126e-f3af-7019-b313-adbb6247fa92 | challenge → be → to develop theoretical models of PD pathogenesis

# sentence: We believe that such models will help interdisciplinary cooperation by helping to structure both the interdisciplinary learning process and the formulation of testable key hypotheses.
019f126e-f3af-7ee9-9a89-9bddb6926b3b | such models → help → interdisciplinary cooperation

# sentence: However, a multifactorial disease such as PD, whose progression is believed to be influenced by the collective action of several genes and environmental factors, cannot be adequately represented by a simple model.
019f126e-f3af-74e0-a280-4f83d6495559 | PD → be → difficult to model

# sentence: The multifactorial nature renders making predictions related to onset and progression a very challenging task.
019f126e-f3af-73e8-b792-b74ffc0c4e1e | multifactorial nature of PD → render → predictions related to onset and progression challenging

# sentence: The progression of the syndrome emerges from the flow of spatiotemporal information between molecular and organic scales.
019f126e-f3af-7431-818b-3ba36eb78f58 | progression of syndrome → emerge from → flow of spatiotemporal information between scales

# sentence: Adequate multiple-scale models, aiming to bring PD research to a more integrated level, should therefore aim to understand the subsystem properties that connect the scales and to incorporate information about as many manageable factors as possible, including environmental factors, genetics, proteomics, metabolomics, cell biology, higher-level physiology, and patient quality of life.

# sentence: Graphical network modeling can provide an adequate view of a dynamic system such as PD, which is defined by the coordinated action of several factors and their local dynamics [111].
019f126e-f3af-7b69-9026-8f9ec2c52bfb | graphical network modeling → provide → adequate view of dynamic system such as PD

# sentence: Wellstead et al. recently described a systems-control approach in which disturbances in energy metabolism act as a driving core module, and serve as an analytical and modeling framework with which to study the pathogenesis of PD [112] [113].
019f126e-f3af-7625-b774-694b6fa053bd | Wellstead et al. → describe → systems-control approach
019f126e-f3af-7cb5-a81c-7e61bea4d94f | disturbances in energy metabolism → act as → driving force for neurodegeneration

# sentence: It is important to keep in mind that energy metabolism is highly integrated with complex cell-to-cell interactions.
019f126e-f3af-70e0-b06d-6ca1a34645a7 | energy metabolism → be highly integrated with → complex cell-to-cell interactions

# sentence: Astrocytes, for example, are closely coupled to neurons, and play a key role in energy metabolism, neurotransmission, and many other neuronal functions [114] [115] [116].
019f126e-f3af-7625-98b5-a0f3827cf9ed | astrocytes → be closely coupled to → neurons
019f126e-f3af-7929-acaf-35045a128bc0 | astrocytes → play → key role in energy metabolism
019f126e-f3af-70e3-9753-50fab6daa633 | astrocytes → play → key role in neurotransmission

# sentence: This is reflected in the concept of the tripartite synapse, describing the importance of bidirectional communication between synapses formed by presynaptic and postsynaptic neurons and astrocytes [117].
019f126e-f3af-7182-81df-6a0e5e520e70 | tripartite synapse → describe → importance of bidirectional communication between astrocytes and neurons

# sentence: A major challenge in the experimental analysis of multifactorial diseases is the extensive phenotypic buffering driven by network robustness.
019f126e-f3af-731c-9389-401b08b86415 | phenotypic buffering → be driven by → redundant and compensatory mechanisms
019f126e-f3af-741a-aa1d-7b9e9cfff81a | phenotypic buffering → be → major challenge in experimental analysis of multifactorial diseases

# sentence: In turn, well-chosen predictions of phenotypic changes need to consider the network context and prior knowledge.
019f126e-f3af-7983-b335-59c664418960 | predictions of phenotypic changes → need to consider → network context
019f126e-f3af-7ba9-8749-c05e26ffc1f6 | predictions of phenotypic changes → need to consider → prior knowledge

# sentence: Detailed knowledge of both biology and systems theory are prerequisites for meaningfully furthering our understanding of PD.
019f126e-f3af-7585-b7a2-cb4cf58c8ecb | detailed knowledge of biology → be → prerequisite for furthering understanding of PD
019f126e-f3af-7a9b-9469-1face37dcdd9 | detailed knowledge of systems theory → be → prerequisite for furthering understanding of PD

# sentence: The main challenge will be to understand the transfer functions that connect the multiple scales involved in PD pathogenesis.
019f126e-f3b0-7006-9155-bedd5f9315d2 | main challenge → be → to understand transfer functions connecting multiple scales in PD pathogenesis

# sentence: We believe that our understanding of the signaling pathways connecting molecular events to clinical traits will have made significant progress in a decade from now.

# sentence: In addition to an appropriate analytical framework, it will be crucial to develop noninvasive experimental approaches for time-resolved analyses in experimental models.

# sentence: Because of the multitude of relevant cellular phenotypes in PD, and the need to understand causality in cellular pathogenesis, we believe that light microscopy applications in systems biology will be a major source of data in time-resolved multifactorial single-cell analysis [118].

# sentence: We also think that the integration of information from different, coordinated experimental approaches, combined with appropriate modeling strategies, will greatly enhance our understanding of PD pathogenesis, as well as the predictive power for early PD diagnosis and personalized identification of underlying disease factors.
019f126e-f3b0-7cee-9056-207dc758c98b | integration of information from different experimental approaches → improve → understanding of causality

# sentence: Currently, genetic testing of patients with PD is already possible, and is acting as a driving force for translational research; the current lack of PD subtypespecific therapies, however, makes the use of such genetic testing disputable [12] [119].
019f126e-f3b0-726f-93e3-403220fc3cef | genetic testing of patients with PD → be → possible
019f126e-f3b0-70c2-9605-3922cbe8db76 | genetic testing → act as → driving force for translational research

# sentence: Preparing for an integrated systems-level understanding of PD is now within reach, but remains an extremely ambitious goal.
019f126e-f3b0-7496-a3ec-5c369d8d2d11 | integrated systems-level understanding of PD → be → within reach
019f126e-f3b0-7861-85c2-04359e11e4d2 | integrated systems-level understanding of PD → remain → extremely ambitious goal

# sentence: We believe that this major endeavor will pave the way for a new era of improved personalized medicine.

# sentence: More short-term goals include improved human cell culture models for genetic and pharmacological screening approaches, and the development of more efficient differentiation methods for patient-derived induced pluripotent stem cells [120], as well as improved animal models for translational research [98].
019f126e-f3b0-7c3e-aa66-b6885ea754c2 | short-term goals → include → improved human cell culture models

# sentence: In ongoing projects, the integration of high-dimensional and nonlinear data is already creating an interesting challenge for data interpretation, and stresses the urgent need to extend the application of systems theory to PD research.

# sentence: Although regenerative medicine aiming to restore dopamine levels in the striatum offers transient relief from at least some clinical symptoms, we believe that systems approaches will allow for the development of increasingly sustainable and personalized disease-modifying therapies..
019f126e-f3b0-77d3-a458-ea35f9015f9d | regenerative medicine → offer → transient relief from symptoms

# sentence: Two centuries after the first detailed clinical description of PD by James Parkinson, and more than a decade after the first identification of genetic factors in this disease, PD research has evolved into a very mature research field, which has developed an arsenal of successfully applied symptomatic treatments.
019f0e7a-1800-7000-0000-000000000001 | PD research → evolve into → very mature research field
019f0e7a-1800-7000-0000-000000000002 | PD research field → develop → arsenal of symptomatic treatments

# sentence: However, causative treatment approaches for PD have not yet become available, and both motor and nonmotor symptoms continue to interfere with patient quality of life.
019f126e-f3b0-7846-ab77-06e40dd027ce | causative treatment approaches for PD → not become available

# sentence: This fact highlights the complexity of this disease, and stresses the need for an intelligible integration of findings from 200 years of PD research.

# sentence: Only a few research fields in translational medicine are more advanced than PD research and hence can serve as role models.
019f126e-f3b0-7252-9fcb-2ff6297219d0 | a few research fields in translational medicine → be more advanced than → PD research

# sentence: Cancer research is certainly one of those.

# sentence: There are two main take-home messages [6] [7]: first, it is crucial to define the signals exchanged between various cell types involved in the disease, and it is important to understand the effects of those signals on the integrated circuits of each of those cell types.

# sentence: Second, to develop accurate disease prognosis and treatment paradigms, it will be crucial to reach a level of mathematical clarity with regard to pathogenesis mechanisms, integrating the conceptual structure of systems theory and the logical coherence of neuroscience.

# sentence: We foresee that PD research will evolve to be an increasingly exact science, in which the growing myriad of measurable phenotypic traits will be understood as manifestations of a small set of key principles.
019f126e-f3b0-7eaa-a038-394ffea0079a | PD research → evolve to be → increasingly exact science

